  {
    "number": 106733,
    "title": "Fix configure.py sysconfig fallback used for Python library path detection",
    "user": "TerryTaoYY",
    "created_at": "2025-12-19T07:50:44",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-19T10:38:45",
    "body": "### Summary\r\n`configure.py:get_python_path()` probes Python’s site-packages via a `python -c` snippet using `site.getsitepackages()`. When that probe fails, it falls back to a `sysconfig.get_path(\"purelib\")` snippet.\r\n\r\nThe fallback snippet was missing a closing `)`, causing the `python -c` call to raise a `SyntaxError` and potentially breaking `./configure` on environments where the fallback path is exercised.\r\n\r\n### Changes\r\n- Fix the sysconfig fallback `python -c` snippet in `configure.py`.\r\n- Add a regression test that forces the `site.getsitepackages()` probe to fail and asserts the corrected sysconfig fallback snippet is used.\r\n\r\n### Testing\r\n- `python3 -m unittest -v configure_test`\r\n\r\n### Notes\r\n- Only the fallback command string is changed; the common `site.getsitepackages()` path is unchanged.",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/106733",
    "files": [
      {
        "filename": "configure.py",
        "additions": 1,
        "deletions": 1
      },
      {
        "filename": "configure_test.py",
        "additions": 50,
        "deletions": 0
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "number": 106703,
    "title": "Upgrade GitHub Actions to latest versions",
    "user": "salmanmkc",
    "created_at": "2025-12-19T00:26:12",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-19T10:38:10",
    "body": "## Summary\n\nUpgrade GitHub Actions to their latest versions for improved features, bug fixes, and security updates.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Action | Old Version(s) | New Version | Release | Files |\n|--------|---------------|-------------|---------|-------|\n| `peter-evans/create-pull-request` | [`84ae59a`](https://github.com/peter-evans/create-pull-request/commit/84ae59a2cdc2258d6fa0732dd66352dddae2a412) | [`98357b1`](https://github.com/peter-evans/create-pull-request/commit/98357b18bf14b5342f975ff684046ec3b2a07725) | [Release](https://github.com/peter-evans/create-pull-request/releases/tag/v8) | release-branch-cherrypick.yml, update-rbe.yml |\n\n## Why upgrade?\n\nKeeping GitHub Actions up to date ensures:\n- **Security**: Latest security patches and fixes\n- **Features**: Access to new functionality and improvements\n- **Compatibility**: Better support for current GitHub features\n- **Performance**: Optimizations and efficiency improvements\n\n### Security Note\n\nActions that were previously pinned to commit SHAs remain pinned to SHAs (updated to the latest release SHA) to maintain the security benefits of immutable references.\n\n### Testing\n\nThese changes only affect CI/CD workflow configurations and should not impact application functionality. The workflows should be tested by running them on a branch before merging.\n",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/106703",
    "files": [
      {
        "filename": ".github/workflows/release-branch-cherrypick.yml",
        "additions": 1,
        "deletions": 1
      },
      {
        "filename": ".github/workflows/update-rbe.yml",
        "additions": 1,
        "deletions": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "number": 106691,
    "title": "Warn users about GPU support on Windows",
    "user": "MERT-CKR",
    "created_at": "2025-12-18T21:53:49",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-19T10:37:42",
    "body": "### Summary\r\nAdds a one-time runtime warning for TensorFlow >= 2.11 on native Windows\r\nto clarify that GPU support is not available, even if CUDA/cuDNN are installed.\r\n\r\n### Motivation\r\nMany Windows users believe their GPU setup is broken when\r\n`tf.config.list_physical_devices(\"GPU\")` returns an empty list.\r\nThis change provides an explicit warning explaining the platform limitation.\r\n\r\nFixes #106684\r\n\r\n### Behavior\r\n- No behavior change in device discovery\r\n- Warning is emitted once per process\r\n- No new dependencies introduced\r\n",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/106691",
    "files": [
      {
        "filename": "tensorflow/python/framework/config.py",
        "additions": 24,
        "deletions": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "number": 106645,
    "title": "Fix TFL to TOSA constant truncation to i48 that broke tosa.greater legalization",
    "user": "deeptanshusekhri",
    "created_at": "2025-12-18T11:09:16",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-19T10:37:06",
    "body": "- removed the legacy code path that truncated every 64-bit TFLite constant down to 48 bits, which produced `tosa.greater` ops whose operands having mismatched integer widths violating the TOSA spec.\r\n\r\n- updated the broadcast-to tests so their CHECK lines now expect i64 constants, as legalization now preserves the original element types all the way through.",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/106645",
    "files": [
      {
        "filename": "tensorflow/compiler/mlir/tosa/tests/tfl-to-tosa-pipeline.mlir",
        "additions": 4,
        "deletions": 4
      },
      {
        "filename": "tensorflow/compiler/mlir/tosa/transforms/legalize_tfl.cc",
        "additions": 0,
        "deletions": 8
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "number": 106638,
    "title": "Fix dynamic batch handling for TFL FullyConnected in TOSA legalization",
    "user": "deeptanshusekhri",
    "created_at": "2025-12-18T10:24:36",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-19T10:36:39",
    "body": "Fixing TFLite to TOSA legalization of `tfl.fully_connected` when the batch dimension is dynamic.\r\n\r\n- The previous code always divided `input_type.getNumElements()` by the filter depth, which returns `0` for partially dynamic tensors, producing reshape shapes like `[0, 512]` and finally a `tosa.reshape` with a 0-sized batch\r\n\r\n- To fix this I am adding a guard the batch computation so that dynamic inputs keep `ShapedType::kDynamic`, allowing the pattern to respect dynamic batch sizes reported in #104313\r\n\r\n- Also adding `test_fullyconnected_dynamic_batch` test to `tfl-to-tosa-pipeline.mlir`, checking the generated `tosa.const_shape` ops and reshape flow to prevent regressions.\r\n\r\nFixes #104313",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/106638",
    "files": [
      {
        "filename": "tensorflow/compiler/mlir/tosa/tests/tfl-to-tosa-pipeline.mlir",
        "additions": 15,
        "deletions": 0
      },
      {
        "filename": "tensorflow/compiler/mlir/tosa/transforms/legalize_tfl.cc",
        "additions": 4,
        "deletions": 1
      }
    ]
  },
